{title: The Line of Shem}
{subtitle: Genesis 11:12; 11:14; 11:15; 1 Chronicles 1:18–24; Luke 3:35–36}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 73}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Bb/D] | [Ab] [Bb] | [Eb] [Bb/D] |
| [Ab] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]When Arpachshad had lived thir-[Bb]ty-five years
[Cm]He became the father of She[Gm]lah
[Ab]A son in the quiet of the [Bb]earth
Carrying the [Ab]weight of Shem
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[Eb]When Shelah had lived thir[Bb]ty [Cm]years
He became the father of E[Gm]ber
[Ab]A link in the chain of [Bb]days
From Noah down to the [Eb]Hebrews
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Shelah, you [Bb]stand between the [Cm]stars
In [Ab]the genealogy of [Eb]faith
Connecting the [Bb]flood to the [Ab]promise
In the [Bb]long and living [Eb][Bb/D][Ab]age
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]After he became the father of E[Bb]ber
[Cm]Shelah lived four hundred and three [Gm]years
And [Ab]had other sons and daugh[Bb]ters
In the shadow of the pa[Eb]triarchs
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]Arpachshad fathered She[Bb]lah
[Cm]And Shelah fathered [Gm]Eber
[Ab]Named in the books of Chron[Bb]icles
And traced in [Eb]Luke's holy list
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
From [Ab]Adam to the King of [Bb]Kings
The line holds [Eb]fast through time
{end_of_verse}
